# Option 2 — Ghost add-row at end of list (Linear/Notion style)

No header chrome at all. The list itself carries the affordance: last row is a
muted "+ New label" ghost row. Archived toggle becomes a tiny footer link.
Description appears only in the empty state.

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ (● Urgent)                                                    ✎  │
│ (● Backlog)                                                   ✎  │
│ (● Blocked)                                                   ✎  │
│ (● Waiting)                                                   ✎  │
│ ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄ │
│  + New label                                  (muted, hover→fg)  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                              Show archived (2) ▾
```

Click ghost row → opens the existing create modal (or later: inline edit row).

Empty state carries the explanation instead of a permanent subtitle:

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                                  │
│        No labels yet.                                            │
│        A shared vocabulary you apply to concepts and items.      │
│                                                                  │
│                        [ + New label ]                           │
│                                                                  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

+ cleanest possible resting state; add-action sits where the result appears
+ same pattern works for Views (ghost card at bottom of the stack)
- "New" less discoverable for first-time admins (mitigated by empty state)
- non-admins just see the list end (ghost row hidden) — fine
